      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: Glad to see a proper response about the problems! Out of curiosity, is the 8kbps supposed to include the doubling up of the data before being sent out? During my own testing I had found that once the data left udon (Including the udon headers), it then had doubled beyond that when actually being sent out. When testing, I had personally found it to begin rate limiting with serializations as low as 4-6kbps (before doubling), which would line up with your 8-12kbps of total data. From the creators side, would that mean that our actual limit where we can expect unthrottled data is 4-6kbps?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
