      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5c9d5c699cbfb22688db5014|full_name}: From what I've been told and understand, there are other rate limits other than total data size like message rates and etc, and you're likely hitting those.\n\nIt is best to encode one big object rather than many small objects more often, as there's overhead per serialization (data size limits) in addition to message rates.\n\nThese rates aren't documented for security reasons.\n\nI will add: it seems that we don't have any documentation on best practices for networking that would include this advice. That's definitely a mistake on our end, and I plan on trying to rectify that as soon as possible.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
